drills.explanation:
Keep registrations per type in order, cache singleton instances per registration, and apply the candidate rules in `get`:

```java
var candidates = regs.getOrDefault(type, List.of());
if (candidates.isEmpty()) throw new IllegalStateException("no bean of type " + type.getSimpleName());
Reg chosen = candidates.size() == 1 ? candidates.get(0) : pickPrimary(candidates);
return type.cast(instance(chosen));
```

`instance` returns the cached object for a singleton (creating it on first use) and calls the factory every time for a prototype. Passing `this` into the factory is how a bean resolves its own dependencies, exactly like constructor injection.

